# Auditing a school-placement route
#
# Sample students, schools, walking distances, and policy limits describe a
# placement problem. N3 rules compare the supplied provisional and audited
# choices and flag excessive walking or a mismatch. They report the supplied
# audit results rather than computing routes or school assignments.

@prefix : <https://eyereasoner.github.io/eyeling/examples/school-placement-audit#> .
@prefix math: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/math#> .
@prefix log: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#> .
@prefix string: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/string#> .

# The companion input supplies provisional and audited choices.
# Flag a recorded walking distance above the policy limit.
{
    ?Student :provisional ?Provisional ;
        :auditedBest ?Audited ;
        :walkingMeters ?Walk .
    :Policy :maxWalkingMeters ?MaxWalking .
    ?Walk math:greaterThan ?MaxWalking .
} => {
    ?Student :auditFlag :walkingLimitExceeded .
} .

# Also flag a provisional school that differs from the supplied audited best.
{
    ?Student :provisional ?Provisional ;
        :auditedBest ?Audited .
    ?Provisional log:notEqualTo ?Audited .
} => {
    ?Student :auditFlag :assignmentDiffersFromAuditedBest .
} .

# Summarize the three named flagged students and compare their supplied
# detours. The suggested assignments in the head are fixed text.
{
    :Ada :auditFlag ?AdaFlag .
    :Bjorn :auditFlag ?BjornFlag .
    :Davi :auditFlag ?DaviFlag .
    :Ada :hiddenDetour ?AdaDetour .
    :Bjorn :hiddenDetour ?BjornDetour .
    :Davi :hiddenDetour ?DaviDetour .
    ?BjornDetour math:lessThan ?AdaDetour .
    ?DaviDetour math:lessThan ?AdaDetour .
} => {
    :Audit :result "fail" ;
        :affectedChildren "Ada, Björn, Davi" ;
        :largestHiddenDetour "Ada, 3000 m" ;
        :recommendedAssignments "Ada -> Lindholmen; Björn -> Backa; Clara -> Haga; Davi -> Haga" .
} .

# Render the audit summary. These rules do not recompute candidate routes;
# they check and report records already provided by the companion input.
{
    :Audit :result ?Result ;
        :affectedChildren ?Affected ;
        :largestHiddenDetour ?Detour ;
        :recommendedAssignments ?Assignments .
    (
        "# school-placement-audit\n\n## Source files\n\n- [N3 rules](../school-placement-audit.n3)\n- [Input TriG](../input/school-placement-audit.trig)\n\n## Answer\naudit result : %s\nchildren affected by straight-line rule : %s\nlargest hidden detour : %s\nrecommended assignments : %s\nexplanation requested : yes\n\n## Explanation\nThe support-tool rule chooses the school with the smallest straight-line distance, using preference rank only as a tie-breaker. The independent audit recomputes each candidate with walking-route distance plus 600 m per preference step. Any provisional assignment that is not the audited best, or that requires more than 2500 m of walking, is flagged. Ada and Björn look close to Centrum on a map, but their walking routes cross barriers and exceed the walking limit; Davi is also better served by the first-preference Haga route. This illustrates why a decision-support label is not enough: route geometry, preferences, and audit records must be inspectable."
        ?Result ?Affected ?Detour ?Assignments
    ) string:format ?Block .
} => {
    :schoolPlacementAudit log:outputString ?Block .
    :schoolPlacementAudit :reports :Audit .
} .
